notions.definition:
**Remember**

**To the retailer**
- breaks bulk, so small quantities can be bought;
- offers a variety of goods from many makers;
- gives credit;
- stores goods and may deliver them;
- gives information and advice on new products.

**To the manufacturer**
- places large orders;
- stores goods, saving warehouse cost;
- pays early, which finances more production;
- bears risks such as a fall in demand;
- passes on market information.
